  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan has a qi path battlefield prepared. When Immortal Crane Sect’s Pine Crane Pavilion flies closer in immemorial white heaven, he activates it and traps Fang Zheng inside. Boundless qi currents gather toward the house. Fang Zheng takes it for a rank eight killer move. At the crucial moment Duke Long appears, having followed secretly, and breaks the surrounding qi currents. Duke Long shouts for the attacker to come out. Fang Yuan reveals himself with a different appearance and names himself Qi Sea Ancestor.",
      "chapters": [
        1833
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "fac_immortal_crane_sect",
        "char_fang_zheng",
        "char_duke_long"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He is an old man in a white robe, sleeves fluttering in the air. His long white beard droops to his feet. He has a solemn expression and a grand aura, with clouds floating quietly around him.",
      "chapters": [
        1834
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Zheng sees an old man in a white robe, sleeves fluttering, a long white beard to his feet, a solemn expression, and clouds around him. Fang Zheng cannot match the face to any known Eastern Sea rank eight expert, and reads rank eight cultivation. Duke Long says that as a rank eight it is fine to call yourself an ancestor, but calling yourself Qi Sea in front of him is too arrogant. Fang Zheng, hearing that, thinks that Duke Long primarily cultivates qi path, followed by transformation path, and that this Eastern Sea old man also cultivates qi path. Fang Yuan, speaking as that identity, calls himself a secluded cultivator of Eastern Sea and says Heavenly Court will look for trouble with him in the future. Duke Long attacks with dragon claw strike. The hit turns the target into cloud fog in the qi path battlefield. Duke Long does not turn around. He points behind him, and air currents form a layer of bubbles around Pine Crane Pavilion. He then pushes with his palms, and multiple qi dragons emerge. Qi Sea Ancestor then sends grand blade qi down from the sky. Duke Long uses qi wall to block that blade.",
      "chapters": [
        1834
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "qi-path-duel",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
